window.docContents[56].resolve({"/rules/RG1002/#RG1002-configuration":{"contents":"No source option, attribute or command-line flag makes this rule pass on a claimed surface. set_option linter.regula false and regula.localFoundation never waive it: lake lint, the build-lint policy target and axiomGate still apply the rule. Where Regula's local linter reports a finding during a project build (axiomGate and the policy target keep it on by default; lake lint builds with it off, whatever the source sets linter.regula to), that finding is a build warning, so the result is INCOMPLETE under RG2003 instead of carrying this rule's finding. Switching the local linter off changes which finding is reported, never whether the result is accepted. Hiding the diagnostic does not establish the property it checks.\n\nProject enforcement runs through lake lint (incremental), lake lint -- --fresh and lake exe axiomGate (fresh whole-project audits from empty build output), and the build-lint policy target. See the adoption guide.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG1002: Proof holes are forbidden","header":"Configuration and exceptions","id":"/rules/RG1002/#RG1002-configuration"},"/rules/RG2001/#RG2001-configuration":{"contents":"There is no configuration that turns an incomplete setup into a pass.\n\nProject enforcement runs through lake lint (incremental), lake lint -- --fresh and lake exe axiomGate (fresh whole-project audits from empty build output), and the build-lint policy target. See the adoption guide.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG2001: The declared Lean environment must be available","header":"Configuration and exceptions","id":"/rules/RG2001/#RG2001-configuration"}});